Task: Install a Mercury/TP-Link AIC8800DC WiFi dongle driver on this Linux Mint XFCE computer.

Setup file: mercury-wifi-installer.tar.gz (522KB) — you'll need to get this file. Options:
  - Download from github.com/Kiborgik/aic8800dc-linux-patched (https://github.com/Kiborgik/aic8800dc-linux-patched) and apply patches, OR
  - The user has the file on a USB stick — copy it to /tmp/ then:

cd /tmp
tar xzf mercury-wifi-installer.tar.gz
cd mercury-wifi-installer
sudo ./install.sh

The script will:
1. Install build tools (build-essential, linux-headers, eject)
2. Fix the interface check in the source
3. Build the driver from source
4. Install firmware + modules
5. Set up usb_modeswitch + udev rule for auto mode-switching
6. Configure auto-load on boot

After install, the dongle will work like built-in WiFi — plug it in, it auto-switches from storage to WiFi mode, driver loads, and it appears in the system tray.
